msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:0
msgid "`StructuredGrid` and `RectilinearGrid`"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:0
msgid "Not implemented"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:0
msgid "No differentiator between the backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:31
msgid "**User choice**: An optional backend lets users trade consistency with VTK for rendering features and quality that three.js offers."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:33
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:35
msgid "Stay vtk.js-only and wait for upstream vtk.js to implement missing VTK features."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:36
msgid "Add three.js as an optional, opt-in rendering backend alongside vtk.js."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:37
msgid "Replace vtk.js with three.js entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:39
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:41
msgid "Chosen option: \"Add three.js as an optional, opt-in rendering backend alongside vtk.js\" (proposed, not yet accepted), because it offers a path to rendering capabilities that vtk.js has not yet implemented from VTK, delivered by translating the PyVista scene into three.js, while preserving the vtk.js path that keeps pyvista-js aligned with desktop VTK semantics. Making three.js opt-in keeps the default behavior unchanged, and lazy-loading the backend keeps the extra bundle cost off users who do not need it."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:43
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:45
msgid "Good, because users get access to rendering capabilities beyond what vtk.js currently implements, delivered through per-feature scene translation work, instead of waiting on upstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:46
msgid "Good, because the default vtk.js path stays intact, so existing users and tests see no behavior change."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:47
msgid "Bad, because rendering-dependent code in `ts/renderer.ts` must be abstracted behind a backend interface, which is real refactoring work."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:48
msgid "Bad, because two backends must be tested against the same scene features, and drift between them is a permanent maintenance tax."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:49
msgid "Bad, because results (camera state, picking, screenshots) may differ subtly between backends unless conformance tests are written."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:51
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:53
msgid "Compliance is confirmed by review of the renderer abstraction and by a conformance test that renders the same scene features on both backends and compares outputs. The ADR status moves from `proposed` to `accepted` or `rejected` after discussion in the PR that carries this record."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:55
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:57
msgid "Stay vtk.js-only"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:59
msgid "Keep the current single-backend architecture and file issues upstream for missing VTK features."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:61
msgid "Good, because there is no new code path, no bundle growth, and no second upstream to track."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:62
msgid "Good, because pyvista-js stays closest to desktop VTK semantics, which is the project's core promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:63
msgid "Bad, because pyvista-js cannot offer VTK features that vtk.js has not implemented, on a timeline pyvista-js does not control."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:65
msgid "Add three.js as an optional backend (proposed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:67
msgid "Implement a small renderer backend interface; vtk.js stays the default, three.js is opt-in and lazy-loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:69
msgid "Good, because rendering capabilities that vtk.js currently lacks can be delivered through three.js translations, instead of users waiting on upstream vtk.js."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:70
msgid "Good, because opt-in plus lazy-loading keeps the default bundle and behavior unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:71
msgid "Good, because the small set of three.js primitive object types keeps the per-feature scene translation simple for the PolyData-style geometry pyvista-js renders today."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:72
msgid "Neutral, because three.js does not implement the VTK pipeline, so the backend must translate PyVista scene descriptions rather than share vtk.js objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:73
msgid "Bad, because it doubles the testing surface and adds a second upstream dependency to track."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:75
msgid "Replace vtk.js with three.js entirely"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:77
msgid "Drop vtk.js and render everything through three.js."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:79
msgid "Good, because there is only one backend and three.js has a very large ecosystem and community."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:80
msgid "Bad, because three.js has no notion of the VTK pipeline, so VTK-specific semantics would have to be rebuilt and would drift from desktop VTK."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0001-add-three-js-rendering-option.md:81
msgid "Bad, because it discards working, tested vtk.js integration for no feature gain on the happy path."
msgstr ""

